  "content": "Flower farmers complain of unfair prices, urge government to fix rates\nOnlinekhabar\nSunday, October 12, 2025\n0\nComments\nKathmandu, October 12\nNepali farmers have complained of not receiving fair prices for marigold garlands and have urged the government to fix rates ahead of Tihar.\nSahadev Basnet, a farmer from Gundu, Bhaktapur, said the value of garlands has declined despite years of hard work. “About 10 years ago, one garland sold for up to Rs 33. Now the price ranges only between Rs 18 and Rs 23,” he said.\nAnother farmer, Ganga Thapa, who has been cultivating marigolds for 20 years, echoed similar concerns. “With such low prices, there is hardly any profit,” she said, urging the government to fix prices just as it sets goat and sheep prices for Dashain.\nShe also complained about poor-quality seeds and pest infestations.\nFarmer Nirmala Basnet noted that demand for garlands has increased this year, with traders visiting homes to buy them directly. “I sold 2,000 garlands last year, and I’ve already sold 1,200 this year,” she said.\nFarmers Radha Thapa and Anita Basnet also complained that the absence of fixed prices benefits only middlemen, leaving both farmers and consumers at a loss. “Middlemen take all the profit. The government must set prices so farmers get fair returns and consumers are not overcharged,” they said.\nReact to this post\nHot Topics\ngold\nnepali cricket\nflood\nSushila Karki\ninsurance\nministers\nICC T20 World Cup Qualifier\nConversation\nNew\nOld\nPopular\nAdd Comment\nLogin to comment\nRemenber me\nForgot password?\nLogin\nNot have account yet?\nSignup Now\nOr use Social Media?\nGoogle\nFacebook\nTwitter\nForgot Password?\nSend Password Reset Link\nBack\nRelated News\nMost Read\nUAE introduces new rules for Visit Visa Sponsorship\n12 stranded backpackers rescued from Langtang\nWhen a joke fuels division: Casual hate speech and the Gen Z revolution in Nepal\nGold price reaches record high at Rs 235,960 per tola\nGold price surges by Rs 10,000 per tola after Dashain\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nSubscribe to Onlinekhabar English to get notified of exclusive news stories.\nEditor's Pick\nEditor's Pick\n4 government buildings, including Supreme Court, declared unfit for use\n3 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nCharred body found at Koteshwor Bhatbhateni, Gen-Z protest death toll rises to 74\n4 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nNo consensus on Hami Nepal’s claim of leading the Gen-Z movement\n4 weeks ago\nEditor's Pick\nDecades-old irrigation projects stall as Madhesh faces drought, food crisis looms\n3 months ago\nEditor's Pick\nNepal’s farming crisis: When plans stay on paper and fields suffer\n3 months ago\nAlso Read\nSociety\nFear among Raute community after drunk intruders enter settlement; security demanded\n3 hours ago\nCricket\nNepal to face UAE in Super Six clash of ICC T20 World Cup Qualifier\n3 hours ago\nOpinion\nThe rise of Nepal’s first woman Prime Minister\n7 hours ago\nPolitics\nWho do student unions stand for? Questions rise after Gen Z Movement\n2 days ago\nEconomy\nThai AirAsia to resume flights from Gautam Buddha International Airport\n2 days ago",
